[
    {
        "text": "Alternative consensus mechanisms were introduced to mitigate these limitations. A prominent alternative consensus mechanism is called proof of stake, which was proposed back in 2011. Proof of stake mechanisms use a pseudo random election process to select validators from a group of nodes. The validators hold and stake the native cryptocurrency of the blockchain in order to validate transactions. Staking refers to the act of validators committing funds to the blockchain network. The locked funds will then act as collateral, meaning malicious validators will mostly likely lose their stake and be kicked out. On the other hand, honest validators will be rewarded as new blocks are produced. Generally, the more coins are staked, the more likely you get to validate a new block and receive rewards.",
        "start": 160,
        "end": 44220,
        "confidence": 0.9893877,
